      <div class="orient-grid">
        <div>
          <h2 class="h-plain">Start here</h2>
          <p>The question on the desk is concrete. What does open-source evidence say about moving a main battle tank from the Los Angeles area to Taiwan end to end? Cover every mode that matters. Cover physical, legal, operational, commercial, and political factors. Include defensive protection requirements along the path — what must be protected, detected, and recovered — not a targeting study.</p>
          <p>The raw material is already on disk. You will not crawl the open web for the graded path. Four workers (or three if time is short) read fixed slices of that warehouse. They return cited bundles. One attended director merges into Obsidian <strong>only through MCP</strong>. You audit a sample. A fresh session answers from the vault alone. Then you freeze a baseline P5 will trust this afternoon.</p>

          <h3>What you leave with</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>An Obsidian vault at <code>Documents\p4-vault</code> with hubs, route spine, and cited content notes</li>
            <li>Proof the director wrote through MCP (receipts + permission snapshot), not by ordinary filesystem edit</li>
            <li>Cold-session answers to four graded queries with wikilinks into the brain</li>
            <li>A human audit sample and one repair cycle</li>
            <li><code>Mission_Brief.md</code>, verifier PASS, and external <code>P4_BASELINE_[TODAY].json</code> for P5</li>
          </ul>

